    "It is not very often that you encounter someone, a software engineer by training and profession, speak with an academic enthusiasm about board games. Video games? Maybe. But board games? It feels like an analogue glitch in a digital universe.",
    "So, sitting in R’s living room overlooking a stone wall draped in bougainvillea, our conversation punctuated by the shrieks of the pressure cooker, I find myself curious to know how it began. How did he acquire the eighty-odd board games arranged slightly haphazardly in a white shelf upstairs? How did he become the host and curator of board-game nights in the community?",
